/P 59 0 R
/T (adding support for custom code extensions, version control, and CI/CD pipelines, narrowing the customization gap with traditional development. At the same time, traditional development is absorbing productivity gains from AI-assisted coding tools, component libraries, and cloud-managed infrastructure, narrowing the speed gap with low-code. Rather than one approach displacing the other, the likely trajectory is convergence: teams will choose the right level of abstraction for each part of a system instead of committing an entire organization to one development philosophy.)
