257 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 60 0 R
/T (Low-code and traditional development address different points on the trade-off curve between speed and control. Low-code accelerates delivery and lowers the technical barrier to building software, at the cost of flexibility and platform independence. Traditional development preserves control and scalability, at the cost of time and specialized resources. The right choice depends on project complexity, performance requirements, budget, in-house technical capacity, and the long-term strategic value of the application. Organizations that assess these factors upfront and remain open to a hybrid strategy are best positioned to choose the approach that fits each project rather than defaulting to a single methodology across the board.)
/E (Low-code and traditional development address different points on the trade-off curve between speed and control. Low-code accelerates delivery and lowers the technical barrier to building software, at the cost of flexibility and platform independence. Traditional development preserves control and scalability, at the cost of time and specialized resources. The right choice depends on project complexity, performance requirements, budget, in-house technical capacity, and the long-term strategic value of the application. Organizations that assess these factors upfront and remain open to a hybrid strategy are best positioned to choose the approach that fits each project rather than defaulting to a single methodology across the board.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
