/Title (development, where engineers write source code by hand using programming languages and frameworks, and low-code development, where applications are assembled visually using pre-built components, drag-and-drop interfaces, and configuration rather than extensive hand-written code. This report compares both approaches across development speed, cost, flexibility, scalability, and governance to help organizations select the right fit for a given project.)
