/Title (Key insight: No single row decides the outcome. Low-code tends to win on speed, learning curve, and maintenance effort; traditional development tends to win on customization, scalability ceiling, and vendor independence. Weigh the factors that matter most for the specific project rather than simply counting advantages.)
