/Title (In practice, manyorganizationsdonot choose one approach exclusively. A common pattern is to)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 512 0 R
/Next 587 0 R
>>
endobj
587 0 obj
<<
/Title (use low-code platforms for internal, low-risk, or fast-changing applications, while reserving traditional development for customer-facing products, core business systems, and components that demand deep customization or high performance. Some teams use low-code to prototype an idea quickly, then rebuild validated features with traditional development once requirements stabilize and scale becomes a priority. This hybrid model captures the speed advantage of low-code without permanently sacrificing the flexibility that traditional development provides.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 512 0 R
/Prev 586 0 R
>>
endobj
