/Title (Key insight: Low-code shifts spending from a large one-time engineering cost to a smaller recurring subscription cost. This can favor low-code for short-lived or uncertain projects, while traditional development may become more economical over multiple years when licensing fees outweigh the original build cost.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 583 0 R
/Prev 680 0 R
>>
